 ## Background
-Points2NeRF was proposed in the paper "Points2NeRF: Generating Neural Radiance Fields from 3D point cloud" [S1]. The work leverages hypernetworks, introduced in [12], and PointNet architecture [31]. It aims to reduce the number of trainable parameters by designing a hypernetwork with smaller parameters compared to training individual NeRFs [S1]. The method represents 3D objects as Neural Radiance Fields, allowing for advantages such as obtaining 3D meshes with colors and predicting inside/outside categories for points from a grid [S1].
+Points2NeRF was proposed in the paper "Points2NeRF: Generating Neural Radiance Fields from 3D point cloud" [S1]. The work leverages hypernetworks, introduced in prior work [S1], and the PointNet architecture [S1]. It aims to reduce the number of trainable parameters by designing a hypernetwork with smaller parameters compared to training individual NeRFs [S1]. The method represents 3D objects as Neural Radiance Fields, allowing for advantages such as obtaining 3D meshes with colors and predicting inside/outside categories for points from a grid [S1].
 
